  "summary": "This malware is delivered via a phishing email impersonating Bank of America. A VBScript within a ZIP file initiates a multi-stage PowerShell execution chain that decodes and runs further scripts, ultimately downloading a legitimate ScreenConnect installer. The malware uses a UAC bypass to silently install ScreenConnect with elevated privileges, then uses SDDL and registry modifications to hide the service and prevent its removal.",
